'''''Artemisia indica''''', the '''Indian wormwood''', is a widespread species of flowering plant in the family [[Asteraceae]].<ref name="FoI" >{{cite web |title=Indian Wormwood |url=http://www.flowersofindia.net/catalog/slides/Indian%20Wormwood.html |date=2023 |website=flowersofindia.net |publisher=Flowers of India |access-date=15 September 2023 |quote=Common name: Indian Wormwood, Mugwort }}</ref> It is native to the Indian Subcontinent (except Bangladesh), mainland Southeast Asia, China (except Xinjiang and Qinghai), Taiwan, the Philippines, Korea, the [[Ryukyu Islands]], and Japan, and it has been introduced to [[Peninsular Malaysia]].<ref name="POWO_179626-1" >{{cite POWO |id=179626-1 |title=''Artemisia indica'' Willd. |access-date=15 September 2023 }}</ref> In the wild it is typically found alongside roads, on slopes, in [[forest edge]]s, and in scrublands at elevations below {{cvt|2000|m}}.<ref name="FoC_200023244" >{{cite web |url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=200023244 |title=五月艾 wu yue ai |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=Flora of China |publisher=efloras.org |access-date=15 September 2023 }}</ref>

==Subtaxa==
The following varieties are accepted:<ref name=" POWO_179626-1" />
*''Artemisia indica'' var. ''dissecta'' {{small|Pamp.}} – [[Assam]]
*''Artemisia indica'' var. ''elegantissima'' {{small|(Pamp.) Y.R.Ling & Humphries}} – northern Pakistan, western Himalayas, southeastern Tibet
*''Artemisia indica'' var. ''indica'' – entire range
*''Artemisia indica'' var. ''kumaonensis'' {{small|(Pamp.) Karthik. & Moorthy}} – western Himalayas
*''Artemisia indica'' var. ''momiyamae'' {{small|(Kitam.) H.Hara}} – [[Honshu]]

